4Proofs.WordCorrect.lemma14_reduce_correct:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.treewidth_le:0"],"kind":"dock","label":"Lemma14.treewidth_le","nodeId":"c:Lax117284.Lemma14","semanticId":"Lax117284.Lemma14.treewidth_le"},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.correct:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.kvec_le_days:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.reduce_polyTime:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.treewidth_le:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax429075.EncodingCorrect:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax429075.SATHard:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax759944.TuringRamPolytimeEquivalence:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:conclusion:Lax117284.Lemma14.perClient_npHard:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Compose the hardness of the source with the reduction.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard","tooltipHtml":"Compose the hardness of the source with the reduction."},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14.correct":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14.correct.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14.correct:conclusion:Lax117284.Lemma14.correct:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The vertex-selection gadget of a colour compels one vertex client of that colour, the\nvalidation day pushes its incidence clients onto their edge days, and the two interaction\nclients, needing half the edge days each, leave one of the two incidence clients of every\nedge unserved. The dummy client blocks exactly the clients parked on a day, so each day\nreduces to its gadget.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14.correct","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14.correct","tooltipHtml":"The vertex-selection gadget of a colour compels one vertex client of that colour, the\nvalidation day pushes its incidence clients onto their edge days, and the two interaction\nclients, needing half the edge days each, leave one of the two incidence clients of every\nedge unserved. The dummy client blocks exactly the clients parked on a day, so each day\nreduces to its gadget."},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14Treewidth.treewidth_le":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14Treewidth.treewidth_le.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14Treewidth.treewidth_le:conclusion:Lax117284.Lemma14.treewidth_le:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The overall conflict graph of the constructed instance has a tree decomposition of width\nfour: on every day the dummy client conflicts with the clients that take no part in the\ngadget and with none that does, so apart from the dummy and the two interaction clients,\nwhich every bag holds, the conflicts that remain are those inside a day's gadget — a vertex\nclient with the selection client of its colour, and a vertex client with one of its own\nincidence clients.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14Treewidth.treewidth_le","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Lemma14Treewidth.treewidth_le","tooltipHtml":"The overall conflict graph of the constructed instance has a tree decomposition of width\nfour: on every day the dummy client conflicts with the clients that take no part in the\ngadget and with none that does, so apart from the dummy and the two interaction clients,\nwhich every bag holds, the conflicts that remain are those inside a day's gadget — a vertex\nclient with the selection client of its colour, and a vertex client with one of its own\nincidence clients."},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Machine.MisFinal.reduce_polyTime":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Machine.MisFinal.reduce_polyTime.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Machine.MisFinal.reduce_polyTime:conclusion:Lax117284.Lemma14.reduce_polyTime:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The reduction is a word RAM program on the zeros and ones of its input: a one-pass tokenizer reads\nthe number of colours, the number of vertices per colour, and the bits of the adjacency matrix; a\nfirst pass over the matrix checks that it is symmetric, has no loop and no edge inside a colour\nclass; a second checks that the graph is regular of a positive degree and has an even number of\nedges, by counting the neighbours of every vertex; and the numbers of the image are then written\ncell by cell, the processing time and the due date of each job being a closed form computed from\nits day and its client: a case analysis on the kind of day — a vertex day, a validation day or the\nday of an edge, whose endpoints are found by scanning the matrix for the corresponding edge — and\non the kind of client. The number of colours and the number of vertices are numbers of the input\nand are bounded by its length, since the image is only written for a graph. A word that is not the\ncode of such a graph is answered with the rejected word. The numbers may be exponential in the\nlength of the input, which the word length of a polynomial-time word RAM accommodates, and\npolynomial time on the word RAM transfers to a Turing machine.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Machine.MisFinal.reduce_polyTime","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Machine.MisFinal.reduce_polyTime","tooltipHtml":"The reduction is a word RAM program on the zeros and ones of its input: a one-pass tokenizer reads\nthe number of colours, the number of vertices per colour, and the bits of the adjacency matrix; a\nfirst pass over the matrix checks that it is symmetric, has no loop and no edge inside a colour\nclass; a second checks that the graph is regular of a positive degree and has an even number of\nedges, by counting the neighbours of every vertex; and the numbers of the image are then written\ncell by cell, the processing time and the due date of each job being a closed form computed from\nits day and its client: a case analysis on the kind of day — a vertex day, a validation day or the\nday of an edge, whose endpoints are found by scanning the matrix for the corresponding edge — and\non the kind of client. The number of colours and the number of vertices are numbers of the input\nand are bounded by its length, since the image is only written for a graph. A word that is not the\ncode of such a graph is answered with the rejected word. The numbers may be exponential in the\nlength of the input, which the word length of a polynomial-time word RAM accommodates, and\npolynomial time on the word RAM transfers to a Turing machine."},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Structural.kvec_le_days":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Structural.kvec_le_days.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Structural.kvec_le_days:conclusion:Lax117284.Lemma14.kvec_le_days:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The dummy client is required on every day, the two interaction clients on half the edge\ndays each, and every other client once; a client other than those three exists only if the\ngraph has a colour class, and then the instance has a day.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Structural.kvec_le_days","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Structural.kvec_le_days","tooltipHtml":"The dummy client is required on every day, the two interaction clients on half the edge\ndays each, and every other client once; a client other than those three exists only if the\ngraph has a colour class, and then the instance has a day."},"p:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.lemma14_reduce_correct":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.lemma14_reduce_correct.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.lemma14_reduce_correct:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.correct:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.lemma14_reduce_correct:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.kvec_le_days:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.lemma14_reduce_correct:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.treewidth_le:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.lemma14_reduce_correct:conclusion:Lax117284.Lemma14.reduce_correct:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"A word encoding an instance in normal form is sent to the code of the constructed instance, and the code determines the instance, so the question about the word is the question about the instance; every other word goes to the rejected word, which is in no language, and is not in the language of the normal form.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.lemma14_reduce_correct","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.lemma14_reduce_correct","tooltipHtml":"A word encoding an instance in normal form is sent to the code of the constructed instance, and the code determines the instance, so the question about the word is the question about the instance; every other word goes to the rejected word, which is in no language, and is not in the language of the normal form."}}},"status":"6 statements; 6 proofs","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"prepared-graph\" width=\"1005\" height=\"492\" viewBox=\"0 0 1005 492\" aria-label=\"Proof dependency graph\" data-layout-digest=\"b1bfbb10874779b2bf21d045fc8899dea1c82436711b035b8a03ab4d65660408\"><defs><marker id=\"graph-arrow-proof-network-b1bfbb10874779b2-statements:Lax117284.Lemma14\" viewBox=\"0 -5 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"0\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" orient=\"auto\" overflow=\"visible\"><path d=\"M1,-4.25 L9,0 L1,4.25 Q3,0 1,-4.25 Z\"/></marker></defs><g data-graph-camera><path class=\"graph-edge-hit\" data-edge-hit=\"e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.correct:0\" d=\"M239.883,119.889 L239.883,202 L215.883,202 L215.883,190\"/><path class=\"graph-edge-hit\" data-edge-hit=\"e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.kvec_le_days:0\" d=\"M303.883,119.889 L303.883,218 L199.883,218 L199.883,190\"/><path class=\"graph-edge-hit\" data-edge-hit=\"e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.perClient_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Lemma14.reduce_polyTime:0\" d=\"M479.883,107.857 L479.883,234 L183.883